# Live central copy

The live version is the branch at https://cursor.com/codebase/julian-holtom. Open that on another machine. Do not keep a newer copy only on this computer.

Before editing, pull that central branch and continue from it.

After each project-file change, commit and push that same branch before the next step. Do not wait until the task is finished.

1. Leave out secrets: `.env`, credentials, tokens, and private keys.
2. Push to the remote whose URL is `origin.cursor.com/julian-holtom/<name>`. That remote is the live one. Track it.
3. Keep an existing GitHub remote, but do not send new work there unless asked.
4. If no central repository exists, create a private one under `julian-holtom` and push the working branch.
5. Do not force-push. Do not change the git user name or email. Use the signed-in Cursor account.

Example: this theme's live branch is `https://origin.cursor.com/julian-holtom/directmx-shopify.git`.
